.TH NEOPOP 1 "September 2025" "Neopop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neopop \- lean Cypher graph populator (wrapper around cypher\-shell)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neopop
[\fIOPTION\fR]... (\-u \fIUSER\fR \-p \fIPASS\fR \-a \fIURL\fR \-d \fIDB\fR) \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.PP
Commands:
.RS
.TP
.B monolithic
[\-\-echo\-cys] [\-\-fail\-fast | \-\-best\-effort] [\-\-clean\-db | \-\-reset\-db] \-\-seed \fIFILE\fR [\-\-stm\-wise]
.TP
.B modular
[\-\-echo\-cys] [\-\-fail\-fast | \-\-best\-effort] [\-\-clean\-db | \-\-reset\-db]
\-\-seed\-grp \fIFILE\fR [\-\-stm\-wise | \-\-pkg\-wise \-\-pkg\-size \fIN\fR] [\-\-seed\-pre \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-seed\-post \fIFILE\fR]
.TP
.B db\-check
.TP
.B db\-clean
.TP
.B db\-reset
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Neopop
executes Cypher workloads against a Neo4j 5 database. It wraps
.BR cypher\-shell (1)
to provide consistent commit models, execution control, and common initialization patterns.
.PP
Two graph seed kinds are supported:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Monolithic:
a single Cypher file (DDL and/or DML) executed statement\-wise. Equivalent to feeding the file directly into
.BR cypher\-shell .
.IP \(bu 2
.B Modular:
a triple of optional pre/post schema files (DDL) and a mandatory pure DML file. Supports statement\-wise and package\-wise commit models.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user =\fIUSER\fR
Database username.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password =\fIPASS\fR
Database password.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address =\fIURL\fR
Bolt URL of the server (e.g. \fBneo4j://localhost:7687\fR).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-database =\fIDB\fR
Target database name.
.PP
\fBNote:\fR global options (\-u/\-p/\-a/\-d) must appear \fIbefore\fR the command.
.SH EXECUTION CONTROL
(Commands \fBmonolithic\fR and \fBmodular\fR only; mutually exclusive.)
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-fast
Abort on first error (default if unspecified).
.TP
.B \-\-best\-effort
Execute all statements, report errors at end.
.SH DATABASE PREPARATION
(Commands \fBmonolithic\fR and \fBmodular\fR only; mutually exclusive.)
.TP
.B \-\-clean\-db
Remove all nodes, relationships, constraints, and indexes before seeding.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-db
Drop and recreate the target database before seeding. Requires access to the \fBsystem\fR database.
.SH ECHOING CYPHER
(Commands \fBmonolithic\fR and \fBmodular\fR only.)
.TP
.B \-\-echo\-cys
Echo \fBcypher\-shell\fR output during seeding to the console (it is always logged to \fBneopop.log\fR). Useful for debugging or verifying Cypher execution.
.SH MONOLITHIC COMMAND
.TP
.B \-\-seed \fIFILE\fR
Input file containing DDL and/or DML statements. \fIFILE\fR may be \fB\-\fR for STDIN.
.TP
.B \-\-stm\-wise
Statement\-wise commit model (default). Each statement runs in its own implicit transaction.
.SH MODULAR COMMAND
.TP
.B \-\-seed\-grp \fIFILE\fR
Pure DML seed file (mandatory). \fIFILE\fR may be \fB\-\fR for STDIN.
.TP
.B \-\-stm\-wise
Statement\-wise commit model (default). Each statement runs in its own implicit transaction.
.TP
.B \-\-pkg\-wise
Package\-wise commit model. Statements from \fB\-\-seed\-grp\fR are grouped into explicit transactions of size \fIN\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-pkg\-size \fIN\fR
Number of DML statements per transaction for package\-wise mode. \fIN\fR \[ge] 2 (1 is not allowed).
.TP
.B \-\-seed\-pre \fIFILE\fR
Executed once before \fB\-\-seed\-grp\fR in a single transaction. DDL only.
.TP
.B \-\-seed\-post \fIFILE\fR
Executed once after \fB\-\-seed\-grp\fR in a single transaction. DDL only.
.SH DATABASE COMMANDS
.TP
.B db\-check
Verifies connectivity to the target database by running a trivial Cypher query (\fBRETURN 1\fR).
.TP
.B db\-clean
Removes all data and schema objects from the target database by:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Batch\-deleting all nodes and relationships
.IP \(bu 2
Dropping all constraints
.IP \(bu 2
Dropping all indexes
.RE
.TP
.B db\-reset
Drops and recreates the target database, then waits until it is online again. Requires access to the \fBsystem\fR database. \fBAll data will be permanently lost.\fR
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Monolithic seed from file
.nf
neopop \-u neo4j \-p secret \-a neo4j://localhost:7687 \-d test \\
  monolithic \-\-seed mixed.cypher
.fi
.TP
Monolithic seed from stdin
.nf
cat mixed.cypher | neopop \-u neo4j \-p secret \-a ... \-d test \\
  monolithic \-\-seed \-
.fi
.TP
Modular seed (statement\-wise)
.nf
neopop \-u neo4j \-p secret \-a ... \-d test \\
  modular \-\-seed\-grp graph.cypher \-\-stm\-wise
.fi
.TP
Modular seed (package\-wise, 500 stmts per tx)
.nf
neopop \-u neo4j \-p secret \-a ... \-d test \\
  modular \-\-seed\-grp graph.cypher \\
          \-\-pkg\-wise \-\-pkg\-size 500
.fi
.TP
Modular seed with schema setup/teardown
.nf
neopop \-u neo4j \-p secret \-a ... \-d test \\
  modular \-\-seed\-pre pre.cypher \\
          \-\-seed\-grp graph.cypher \\
          \-\-seed\-post post.cypher \\
          \-\-pkg\-wise \-\-pkg\-size 1000
.fi
.TP
Reset database before running workload
.nf
neopop \-u neo4j \-p secret \-a ... \-d test db\-reset
.fi
